{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>Mahlon and Chilion.</b> We do not know the circumstances for which they were so named, as with Issachar and also Moses. And in the derash it says that they are Yoash and Saraf, because they took Moabite daughters. (1 Chronicles 4:22) And there it is written 'who married Moabite women.' And Moabite women are permitted to Israel, for Scripture forbade only Ammonite and Moabite men, that they may not enter the assembly, and that they may not take Israelite daughters. And in the book of Ezra I will explain this well." "<b>And the meaning of 'of Bethlehem' a second time</b> is to inform that they are natives. And furthermore because it says 'Ephrathites,' and this word sometimes denotes affiliation with the place called Ephrat, and once with the family of Ephraim. And Ephrat is the name of the wife of Caleb son of Hezron, and the place was named after her, like Mitzrayim [Egypt]. And it is not possible that Mahlon and Chilion took these women until they converted, and the proof is 'to her people and to her Elohim.'"], :book :ruth, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Ruth -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/ruth"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:43:20.923027913Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}